From 7a05073b02d85f35c35f8305d496ddf6e991f30f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM: cgroup: prevent spurious transition into non-frozen state

Backport the missing ptrace_stop() hunk from the upstream cgroup freezer
race fix. The companion cgroup_leave_frozen() implementation hunk from
the same upstream commit is already present in this SM8350 tree, so it is
intentionally not duplicated here.

The relevant upstream change reserves cgroup_leave_frozen(true) for
terminating processes and uses false when ptrace_stop() resumes from the
freezer wait. This prevents a task that is still meant to remain frozen
from spuriously decrementing the cgroup frozen-task counter.

Upstream:
  LineageOS/android_kernel_qcom_sm8150
  7a05073b02d85f35c35f8305d496ddf6e991f30f
  "UPSTREAM: cgroup: prevent spurious transition into non-frozen state"

Backported only the missing hunk for the OnePlus SM8350 Linux 5.4 tree.

---
diff --git a/kernel/signal.c b/kernel/signal.c
--- a/kernel/signal.c
+++ b/kernel/signal.c
@@ -2219,7 +2219,7 @@
 		cgroup_enter_frozen();
 		preempt_enable_no_resched();
 		freezable_schedule();
-		cgroup_leave_frozen(true);
+		cgroup_leave_frozen(false);
 	} else {
 		/*
 		 * By the time we got the lock, another tracer may come.
